<title>BELGIUM: Generale lends Vasco  $2.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Generale lends Vasco  $2.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. data security firm Vasco Corp said on Tuesday it had received a $2.5 million bridge loan from Belgium's Generale Bank to help finance the company's operational activities and the commercialization of products.</p>
<p>The loan is in the form of a convertible note with a 3.25 percent coupon. The note may be converted into Vasco common stock at a discount based on the timing of a secondary stock offering.</p>
<p>Generale Bank had a long banking relationship with Digipass nv/sa, a Belgian-based company that Vasco acquired last year, Vasco said.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
